# Delta firmware update for the DWM3001CDK: the halves that live in flash.
#
# This board cannot do a conventional over-the-air update and the arithmetic is
# not close. Two full slots want 844 KB of a 512 KB part; an LZMA-compressed
# secondary still wants ~646 KB; and there is no external flash to stage into.
# What fits is a delta -- 10,906 B measured between two adjacent builds of this
# image. See internal/cdk-ble-ota-plan.md.
#
# The two symbols below are deliberately separate and are never both set on one
# image. The applier goes in the BOOTLOADER, because an application cannot
# rewrite the flash it is executing from. The receiver goes in the APPLICATION,
# because the bootloader has no radio.

config WOZ_DFU_APPLIER
	bool "Delta patch applier (bootloader side)"
	depends on FLASH
	help
	  Compile the detools in-place patch applier and run it from a SYS_INIT
	  at APPLICATION level, which is after the flash driver is up and before
	  MCUboot's own main().

	  Set this ONLY on the MCUboot image. On the application it would link a
	  patcher that can never safely run.

	  MEASURED at 3,176 B of bootloader flash (29,380 -> 32,556 B), which is
	  why firmware/pm_static.yml gives MCUboot 0xA000 rather than the 0x8000
	  it needed before: 0x8000 would have left 212 B free.

	  Nothing happens at boot unless a valid header is found in the
	  patch_staging partition, so the cost on a normal boot is one word read.

if WOZ_DFU_APPLIER

config WOZ_DFU_APPLIER_LOG
	bool "Print applier progress"
	depends on PRINTK
	help
	  Bench only. MCUboot on this board is built with CONFIG_PRINTK=n and no
	  LOG (firmware/sysbuild/mcuboot.conf explains what that is worth), so
	  turning this on also means turning those back on and finding the flash
	  for them.

	  Worth it exactly once: the first time a patch is applied on hardware,
	  when the difference between "declined the patch" and "applied it and
	  produced an image that fails validation" is otherwise invisible.

config WOZ_DFU_APPLIER_CHUNK
	int "Patch read buffer, bytes"
	default 256
	range 64 1024
	help
	  How much of the staged patch is read from flash at a time before being
	  handed to detools. Larger is marginally faster and costs BSS. detools
	  itself is a streaming decoder and imposes no minimum.

endif # WOZ_DFU_APPLIER
